DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__aarraannggee__bb() adds an address range entry to a producer
     instance.

     Argument _d_b_g should reference a DWARF producer instance allocated using
     dwarf_producer_init(3) or dwarf_producer_init_b(3).

     Argument _s_t_a_r_t specifies the relocatable start address of the address
     range.

     Argument _l_e_n_g_t_h specifies the length of the address range.

     Argument _s_y_m_b_o_l___i_n_d_e_x specifies the ELF symbol index of the first symbol
     to be used for relocation.

     Argument _e_n_d___s_y_m_b_o_l___i_n_d_e_x specifies the ELF symbol index of the second
     symbol to be used for relocation.

     ••   If argument _e_n_d___s_y_m_b_o_l___i_n_d_e_x is not 0, the
         DW_DLC_SYMBOLIC_RELOCATIONS flag should have been set on the DWARF
         producer instance.  The address value specified by argument _s_t_a_r_t
         will be treated as an offset value from the first symbol, and the ar‐
         gument _o_f_f_s_e_t___f_r_o_m___e_n_d___s_y_m_b_o_l should hold an offset value from the
         second symbol.  Application code can retrieve the relocation entries
         for the symbol pair by calling function dwarf_get_relocation_info(3).
         The relocation entry for the first symbol will have type
         dwarf_drt_first_of_length_pair and the relocation entry for the sec‐
         ond symbol will have type dwarf_drt_second_of_length_pair.

     ••   If argument _e_n_d___s_y_m_b_o_l___i_n_d_e_x is 0, argument _o_f_f_s_e_t___f_r_o_m___e_n_d___s_y_m_b_o_l
         will be ignored and only one symbol is used for relocation.

     If argument _e_r_r is not NULL, it will be used to store error information
     in case of an error.

     Function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__aarraannggee() is deprecated.  It is similar to function
     ddwwaarrff__aadddd__aarraannggee__bb() except that it cannot handle all possible symbol in‐
     dex values and supports only one relocation symbol.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On success, these functions return a non-zero value.  In case of an er‐
     ror, these functions return 0 and set the argument _e_r_r.

EERRRROORRSS
     These functions can fail with:

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]  Argument _d_b_g was NULL.

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]  Argument _e_n_d___s_y_m_b_o_l___i_n_d_e_x was non-zero, but the flag
                        DW_DLC_SYMBOLIC_RELOCATIONS was not set on the pro‐
                        ducer instance.

     [DW_DLE_MEMORY]    An out of memory condition was encountered during the
                        execution of the function.

